// Boiler power availability, used as an HDO indicator.
//
// This item previously pointed at mqtt:topic:bojler_switch:status, a channel
// that never existed on the thing, so it rendered as a blank line in the
// sitemap. Repointed at the new availability channel, which is what it was
// presumably always meant to show.
//
// Caveat: offline means "zigbee2mqtt cannot reach the switch". On this circuit
// that is almost always HDO being off, but a flat battery, a failed device or a
// zigbee dropout look identical. Treat it as "no power to the switch", not as a
// direct reading of the HDO relay.
String wheater_status "HDO [MAP(hdo.map):%s]" { channel="mqtt:topic:bojler_switch:availability" }

// Co bojler doopravdy dělá, dohromady ze spínače a z napájení.
//
// bojler_switch sám o sobě říká "naposledy zapnuto", ne "zrovna hřeje".
// Zásuvka hlásí stav jen dokud je online, a openHAB navíc zapisuje povel
// optimisticky (autoupdate), takže když HDO odpadne, položka zamrzne na ON a
// vypadá to, že bojler hřeje bez proudu. Odvozuje to rules/boiler_state.rules;
// vlastní spínač zůstává beze změny, protože ho ovládá TimerJob.
String bojler_state "Bojler [%s]"
